# Slice 296 probe (ABSENT-HEAD-WRITE-NORM): an expression as the written content (`x: a + 2`, x bound by nothing) -- a named
# Structure too, so `return: x` in an int fn is refused by the general rule, as with a name or a literal.
fn: f () int
    int: a 1
    x: a + 2
    return: x
end: f
int: code 7
int: v f()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
